{
  peppy_schema: "contract/v1",
  manifest: {
    name: "range_sensor",
    tag: "v1",
    description: [
      "A range sensor: a device or a simulated sensor that streams readings, each one range along a cone, such as an ultrasonic sensor or a time-of-flight sensor with one beam. A sensor that measures a fan of rays in one plane implements lidar_2d, and one that measures in three dimensions implements lidar_3d.",
      "Conventions, the same for every implementer. The fields of a reading are those of ROS's Range that the range sensor layer and the collision monitor of Nav2 read, each with its unit in its name.",
      "Sensor frame. Fixed to the sensor: +X along the axis of the cone, +Y left and +Z up. Only the sensor's own geometry is here: where the sensor sits on a robot is not the sensor's to know, and sensor_mounts gives the pose of this frame on the robot.",
      "Readings. A reading is one message. Its range is the distance (m) from the origin of the sensor frame to the nearest surface the sensor met inside its cone, which opens field_of_view_rad about +X: that surface stands at the range, at most half of field_of_view_rad from +X. A range of 0 marks a reading that the sensor could not measure and a surface nearer than min_range_m; a sensor that cannot tell a reading that met nothing from a reading it could not measure gives 0 for both. A range of 10000 marks a reading that met nothing within max_range_m; max_range_m is below 10000, so a consumer reads every range above max_range_m as that mark. Every other range lies within min_range_m and max_range_m, and every range is a finite number. A sensor that tells only whether a surface stands within one distance has min_range_m equal to max_range_m, and its range is that distance when it detects a surface and 10000 when it detects none. Timestamps are on the clock the implementer's instance reads, the simulation clock in a simulation, and give the time of the measurement, which is earlier than its arrival at the implementer.",
    ],
  },
  interfaces: {
    topics: [
      {
        name: "range_stream",
        description: "The readings of the sensor, as it measures them.",
        qos_profile: "sensor_data",
        message_format: {
          header: {
            $type: "object",
            timestamp: { $type: "time", $description: "When the sensor measured the reading." },
            frame_id: { $type: "u32", $description: "The capture counter of the reading, not a coordinate frame." },
          },
          field_of_view_rad: { $type: "f32", $description: "The full angle of the cone (rad), above 0 and at most pi." },
          min_range_m: { $type: "f32", $description: "The nearest range the sensor measures (m), 0 or above." },
          max_range_m: { $type: "f32", $description: "The farthest range the sensor measures (m), at least min_range_m and below 10000." },
          range_m: { $type: "f32", $description: "The range of the reading (m); 0 and 10000 are the two marks of the contract's description." },
        },
      },
    ],
  },
}
